        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 2:04PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 204 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong
thunderstorms extending from 10 miles northeast of Mesita to 14 miles
southeast of Mesita, moving east at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Tohajiilee and Paguate.

This includes Interstate 40 between Mile Markers 122 and 142.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.

Heavy rains from severe thunderstorms can produce sudden and
dangerous flows in arroyos, ditches and over low water crossings. Do
not attempt to drive through areas where water covers the roadway.</instruction>
